    "narrative": "Our lineup construction today leans heavily into efficiency, prioritizing players with high-upside speed profiles against vulnerable starters. **Corbin Carroll** (74.65) is our undeniable cornerstone; he\u2019s essentially \"cheat code\" status today, boosted by an 86% SB success rate against Gausman\u2019s slow delivery, coupled with a prime #2 slot. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23) is a strong play as he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Kelly (5.27 xERA). His +19% SP skill adjustment highlights the discrepancy between his current form and the opposing mound presence, making him an anchor for both average and power today.\n\nThe volatility of our middle-of-the-pack starters is mitigated by favorable environmental factors. **Max Muncy** (61.65) sneaks into the \"Strong\" category primarily due to a 10% park boost, which overrides the minor platoon penalty he carries against Matthews. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (57.96) remains a volatile but necessary inclusion; despite facing a capable arm in Cavalli, his +14% dynamic platoon edge against the RHP keeps his ceiling high enough to start over lower-scoring bench alternatives. Conversely, **Zach McKinstry** (41.67) barely survives the cut; he stays in the lineup only because of favorable wind conditions providing a marginal lift to his base projection. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Griffin Conine**, who posted a 35.12 score but was ultimately squeezed out. While his xwOBA remains attractive, his position in the bottom of the order and a restrictive platoon disadvantage against Suarez created a clear barrier to entry. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor** closely. **Gabriel Moreno** is slated to hit third, but he faces a tough assignment in Gausman, while **Josh Naylor** faces the elite arm of Wheeler, which severely hampered his score to a marginal 46.99. Owners should keep an eye on official lineups, as any shift down the order for these two could necessitate a pivot to deeper reserve options if defensive or efficiency gaps widen.",
